# Semgrep scan scope (backlog #10). SAST looks at OUR code for injection / XSS / hardcoded
# secrets — a different layer than `npm audit` (which only checks dependencies). Test files are
# EXCLUDED: they legitimately contain example tokens and escaping-assertion fixtures that semgrep
# mistakes for real findings (verified 2026-08-15 on ReplyFlow — 2 of 3 findings were a test's
# `ya29…EXAMPLE…` token and an XSS-escaping test assertion). Scan real code only.
*.test.ts
*.test.tsx
*.test.mjs
*.test.js
*.spec.ts
*.spec.tsx
*_test.ts
__tests__/
test/
tests/
e2e/
*.stories.tsx
*.stories.ts
# build output + vendored code (semgrep skips node_modules by default; listed for clarity)
dist/
build/
node_modules/
coverage/
